#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""accel-advisor — what stands between your design and known-correct acceleration.

The nvc --accel path runs RTL through yosys synthesis (gen_statemachine) plus
equivalence checking, so a chunk that installs and verifies is KNOWN-CORRECT:
proven equivalent to the interpreted semantics, not "probably right".  This
tool reports, per module, exactly which catalog class blocks / degrades /
risks that guarantee, with the evidence and the change that fixes it.

Stages (see regress/tools/README-advisor.md and the campaign log):
  0  environment + flow audit                     (always)
  1  static source scan                           (always)
  2  yosys quick-synth diagnostics per module     (always; memory pre-gate)
  3  nvc accel dry-run, stderr classification     (--run)
  4  correctness probes: VERIFY / X-detect        (--verify)

Exit codes: 0 all candidates ACCELERABLE; 1 BLOCKED present; 2 RISK present
on an installed chunk; 3 tool/flow error.
"""

import argparse, json, os, re, shutil, subprocess, sys, tempfile
from collections import defaultdict

